realboot: PASS and the launch was RECORDED where a REBOOT can find it again: the favourites file on the ext4 root names /bin/hamfmscene. It is $HOME/.hamde/favourites with $HOME resolved by lib/homedir.ad, and on this machine that is /home/live -- rc.5 starts the DE as uid 0, /etc/passwd has no uid 0, so the resolver's last resort is what every DE client gets (/bin/hamfmscene cat: cannot open /root/.hamde/favourites: No such file or directory )
realboot: PASS THE FAVOURITE SURVIVED A REBOOT: on the FIRST click of a fresh boot of the same disk, row 1 of the menu is a section header (85%, 0% category button) where the same rectangle on the machine with no launch history was 0% header and 77% category button. The recency list outlived the menu process, the session AND the power cycle.

