--- FINDING 1, NOW FIXED -- kept because the guest is still asked
    scripts/hamlinux_image.sh staged /etc by a list of FILES:
      for f in hostname hosts passwd ... hamde ...; do [ -f "etc/$f" ] && install ...; done
    etc/hamde is a DIRECTORY, so [ -f ] was false and /etc/hamde/apps --
    the 26 .desktop launchers -- was on NO hamnix-linux machine. Both
    menus fell back to a list compiled into them, in which 5 of 11
    entries named programs no image builds (/bin/calculator,
    /bin/hamterm, /bin/hamedit, /bin/hamview, /bin/hamfm) -- rows that
    did nothing at all when a person clicked them.
    The catalogue is staged now, its 23 remaining programs are built and
    packaged, and a launcher whose program is absent is dropped from the
    menu AND NAMED (appmenu-missing). tests/linux/de_appmenu_installed.sh
    is the gate; what THIS guest found is printed rather than assumed:
        File: /etc/hamde
    (an EMPTY line there means the catalogue is still missing on this
     machine, and every row below it came from the fallback.)
    This gate launches Files -> /bin/hamfmscene, read from files.desktop.

